      "explanation": "Ligand concentration is maximum when the reaction has not been initiated. At that point, absorption of light by ligands will be maximum. As the reaction starts, ligand concentration decreases so is the absorption of light till the point where all the metal ions are consumed and further complex formation does not take place.\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3pcty1x/76c7196c-ef62-4036-abde-f98a176da2a5/0aa67d50-de3c-11ec-8d15-d70e976d6a92/file-1l3pcty1y.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3pcty1x/76c7196c-ef62-4036-abde-f98a176da2a5/0aa67d50-de3c-11ec-8d15-d70e976d6a92/file-1l3pcty1y.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Online) 16th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Practical Organic Chemistry Question 108 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3pcty1x/76c7196c-ef62-4036-abde-f98a176da2a5/0aa67d50-de3c-11ec-8d15-d70e976d6a92/file-1l3pcty1y.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3pcty1x/76c7196c-ef62-4036-abde-f98a176da2a5/0aa67d50-de3c-11ec-8d15-d70e976d6a92/file-1l3pcty1y.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3pcty1x/76c7196c-ef62-4036-abde-f98a176da2a5/0aa67d50-de3c-11ec-8d15-d70e976d6a92/file-1l3pcty1y.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3pcty1x/76c7196c-ef62-4036-abde-f98a176da2a5/0aa67d50-de3c-11ec-8d15-d70e976d6a92/file-1l3pcty1y.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3pcty1x/76c7196c-ef62-4036-abde-f98a176da2a5/0aa67d50-de3c-11ec-8d15-d70e976d6a92/file-1l3pcty1y.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3pcty1x/76c7196c-ef62-4036-abde-f98a176da2a5/0aa67d50-de3c-11ec-8d15-d70e976d6a92/file-1l3pcty1y.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720